WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.942
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level one.

2
00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:09.582
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:14.729
Unit six: Education News. Today you will give updates with the present perfect.

4
00:00:15.029 --> 00:00:17.461
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.366
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.217 --> 00:00:23.102
Curriculum.

7
00:00:24.117 --> 00:00:27.277
Curriculum means the subjects taught in a school or course.

8
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:30.603
The new curriculum includes computer skills.

9
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:33.846
Your turn. Say: Curriculum.

10
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.713
Curriculum.

11
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:39.312
Enrollment.

12
00:00:40.317 --> 00:00:43.350
Enrollment means the number of students who join a school.

13
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.391
Enrollment rose by ten percent this year.

14
00:00:46.983 --> 00:00:49.276
Your turn. Say: Enrollment.

15
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.169
Enrollment.

16
00:00:53.917 --> 00:00:55.092
Scholarship.

17
00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:59.639
Scholarship means money given to a student to pay for study.

18
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.331
She won a scholarship to university.

19
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:05.256
Your turn. Say: Scholarship.

20
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.380
Scholarship.

21
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:11.315
Graduation.

22
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:15.976
Graduation means the ceremony when a student completes a course.

23
00:01:16.583 --> 00:01:18.478
Parents cheered at the graduation.

24
00:01:19.083 --> 00:01:21.968
Your turn. Say: Graduation.

25
00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:26.055
Graduation.

26
00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:28.027
Policy reform.

27
00:01:29.017 --> 00:01:32.467
Policy reform means an official change to make a system better.

28
00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:35.954
The policy reform gave schools more teachers.

29
00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.585
Your turn. Say: Policy reform.

30
00:01:42.433 --> 00:01:43.841
Policy reform.

31
00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:45.875
Literacy rate.

32
00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:50.473
Literacy rate means the percentage of people who can read and write.

33
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:53.362
The literacy rate has risen steadily.

34
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.614
Your turn. Say: Literacy rate.

35
00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:00.874
Literacy rate.

36
00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:02.455
Funding.

37
00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.494
Funding means money provided for a particular purpose.

38
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:10.232
Extra funding built twelve new classrooms.

39
00:02:10.817 --> 00:02:13.109
Your turn. Say: Funding.

40
00:02:15.967 --> 00:02:16.910
Funding.

41
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:18.639
Access.

42
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:22.660
Access means the ability to reach or use something.

43
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.888
Rural children need better access to schools.

44
00:02:26.483 --> 00:02:29.136
Your turn. Say: Access.

45
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:32.966
Access.

46
00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:37.243
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:42.535
Visal, an article says 'Enrollment has risen this year.' Why not 'rose'?

48
00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:52.688
The present perfect links a past change to now. Education news often reports progress that continues to affect schools today.

49
00:02:53.783 --> 00:02:55.527
So it is good for updates?

50
00:02:56.617 --> 00:03:08.023
Yes. 'The government has announced a policy reform' is new information, and 'has introduced', 'has increased' and 'has not yet' are common patterns.

51
00:03:09.117 --> 00:03:11.209
When do I switch to the past simple?

52
00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:22.620
When you give a finished time or detail: 'It announced the reform on Monday.' The first sentence is news; the second adds the facts.

53
00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.488
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.940
Grammar focus: Present perfect for news updates.

55
00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.450
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.637
Enrollment has risen by ten percent this year.

57
00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.502
The government has announced a major policy reform.

58
00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:41.881
Many schools have received extra funding.

59
00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:50.942
Use the present perfect for recent news and changes that still matter. Do not add a finished time: say 'has announced', not 'has announced yesterday'.

60
00:03:51.683 --> 00:03:55.450
Be careful! Don't say: Enrollment has risen last year.

61
00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.539
Say: Enrollment rose last year.

62
00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.570
Do not use the present perfect with 'last year'.

63
00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:06.344
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:08.483
Schools in the News.

65
00:04:08.783 --> 00:04:12.535
Education news tracks how well a country prepares its young people.

66
00:04:13.533 --> 00:04:18.853
This year enrollment has risen, and many students have received a scholarship for further study.

67
00:04:19.867 --> 00:04:23.921
The government has also introduced a policy reform to update the curriculum.

68
00:04:24.933 --> 00:04:29.708
Extra funding has helped rural schools, so access to education is slowly improving.

69
00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.791
As a result, the literacy rate has continued to grow.

70
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.855
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:39.717 --> 00:04:42.181
Enrollment blank by ten percent this year.

72
00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:46.180
A, has risen. B, rised. C, have rose.

73
00:04:49.733 --> 00:04:51.443
The answer is A: has risen.

74
00:04:52.583 --> 00:04:55.709
Money given to a student to pay for study is a blank.

75
00:04:56.009 --> 00:05:00.487
A, curriculum. B, scholarship. C, funding rate.

76
00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:06.103
The answer is B: scholarship.

77
00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:10.248
The percentage of people who can read and write is the blank.

78
00:05:10.548 --> 00:05:14.399
A, literacy rate. B, enrollment. C, graduation.

79
00:05:17.933 --> 00:05:20.072
The answer is A: literacy rate.

80
00:05:21.217 --> 00:05:22.845
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:23.145 --> 00:05:30.281
A, The government has announced it yesterday.. B, The government has announced a reform.. C, The government have announce a reform..

82
00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:36.959
The answer is B: The government has announced a reform..

83
00:05:38.117 --> 00:05:41.068
According to the reading, extra funding has helped…

84
00:05:41.368 --> 00:05:45.846
A, city schools. B, rural schools. C, private schools.

85
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.736
The answer is B: rural schools.

86
00:05:52.933 --> 00:05:56.050
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:56.917 --> 00:05:59.926
What education news story would you like to read more about?

88
00:06:08.717 --> 00:06:10.426
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:10.726 --> 00:06:30.578
I would like to read more about scholarships for students in rural areas. Many talented young people cannot continue their studies because their families lack money. News about funding and access could show which programmes are working. It could also encourage more organisations to help.

90
00:06:30.878 --> 00:06:32.645
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:38.397
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect for news updates.

92
00:06:38.697 --> 00:06:44.170
Today's value is educational equity. Every learner deserves a fair chance to succeed.

93
00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:47.006
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.866
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

